Q: In a C++ class, how do I declare friendship with a templated function in another namespace? A: <p>There is a parsing &quot;issue&quot; with:</p>
<pre><code>template &lt;typename T&gt; friend T ::ns::foo(int);
</code></pre>
<p>Whereas you add space to separate thing, it is interpreted as:</p>
<pre><code>template &lt;typename T&gt; friend (T::ns::foo)(int);
</code></pre>
<p>You have to use parenthesis:</p>
<pre><code>template &lt;typename T&gt; friend T (::ns::foo)(int);
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://godbolt.org/z/YK8P86G4r" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
